🐛 Category 2: Section Boundaries Not Detected (Content Over-Extraction)  ✅ SOLVED (2026-05-13)

Root cause: Two independent bugs in `pipeline.py`:
1. Pre-heading metadata (author, doc number, affiliations) on page 0 was not
   stripped from the body after extraction into YAML, causing duplicate metadata
   in the Markdown output.
2. The `_TOC_BODY_PROTECT_MIN_WORDS` filter applied its word-count gate to
   every paragraph after a protected heading. Short but valid prose paragraphs
   (e.g. "Finally, a plan for progress is outlined (§5).") were stripped as
   suspected TOC artifacts.

Fix:
1. Added pre-heading metadata stripping: after metadata merge, all non-heading
   sections on page 0 before the first HEADING/TITLE are removed from the
   section list.
2. Refined min_words logic: the word-count gate now applies only to the first
   body paragraph after a protected heading. Once that first paragraph confirms
   the section has real content, all subsequent paragraphs are protected
   regardless of length.

