🐛 Category 3: Numbered Headings Ignored by Parser  ✅ SOLVED (2026-05-13)

Root cause: MuPDF splits heading blocks so the section number ("1") and title
("Abstract") are on separate lines within the same block, both at the same font
size and weight. `_render_heading_spans` in `emit.py` only rendered `lines[0]`,
silently dropping the title text. `_split_heading_body` did not split because
both lines had identical font properties. `_merge_orphan_heading_numbers` did
not trigger because `sec.text` contained both lines (not bare number).

Fix: Modified `_render_heading_spans` to detect bare section numbers on line 0
(via `_BARE_HEADING_NUM_RE`) and join subsequent same-font lines to recover the
title text. Golden tests updated for p1068r11 (Roman numerals) and p3556r0
(decimal numbered headings).

Verified: P4161R0 regenerated with correct headings (e.g. `### 1 Abstract`).
P4160R0 and N5034 were already correct (different heading patterns).

