🐛 Category 4: Empty or Partially Extracted Abstract (Under-Extraction)  ✅ SOLVED (2026-05-13)

Root cause: MuPDF merged the bold "Abstract" heading and its non-bold body
paragraph into a single block because they are spatially adjacent. Both use
fs=12.0pt (body size). `_split_heading_body` in `structure.py` has a
`bold_drop` condition that should split bold-heading + non-bold-body, but
it required `fs0 >= body_size * 1.05` (the `_HEADING_SIZE_RATIO` guard).
At body font size (12.0 < 12.6), the guard blocked the split. The entire
7-line block stayed as one HEADING section, and `_render_heading_spans`
rendered only line[0] ("Abstract"), silently dropping lines 1-6 (the prose).

Fix: Relaxed the `bold_drop` guard in `_split_heading_body` to also trigger
when line0 is short (<= `_HEADING_MAX_WORDS` = 12 words), regardless of
font size ratio. This catches bold headings at body size while preserving
the size-ratio guard for longer bold lines (preventing false splits on bold
paragraph starts).

