🐛 Category 7: Duplicate & False-Positive Headings (Running Header Leakage)

Root cause (debugged 2026-05-13): Some LaTeX-generated PDFs (e.g. P4012R0)
include per-page running headers that repeat the current section name in normal
font size (9.7pt). These are distinct from the actual section headings which
use large CAPS font (19.9pt). `structure_sections` classifies both as headings
because both start with a section number, producing duplicate headings:
  - `## 5 Motivation` (running header, LOW confidence, 9.7pt)
  - `### 5 MOTIVATION` (real heading, MEDIUM confidence, 19.9pt)

Additionally, footnote/margin text starting with a number (8.9pt) gets
false-positive promoted to headings:
  - `## 2 format strings are very close, though: https://...`
  - `## 3 explicit conversion to basic_vec allows conversions...`

This causes the markdown viewer's auto-generated Table of Contents to display
broken entries (bare numbers like "1", "2", "3" without titles, plus long
body-text lines promoted to headings).

Proposed fix (two parts):
1. Heading dedup: when two consecutive headings have the same normalized text
   (case-insensitive, after stripping section number prefix), keep only the one
   with higher confidence. This removes running-header duplicates.
2. False-positive filter: headings with LOW confidence and font size below body
   size should be demoted to PARAGRAPH. This removes footnote/margin text.

Both fixes would go in `structure.py` or as post-processing in `pipeline.py`.

Affected Papers (confirmed):

  - P4012R0 (23 headings produced, only 12 are real; 11 are running headers
    or false positives)

🐛 Category 7b: Multi-Font Heading Recovery (Extension of Category 3)

Root cause (debugged 2026-05-13): Some LaTeX templates (Matthias Kretz simd
papers) use a decorative two-font heading pattern: a large bold number
(EURB10, 19.9pt) paired with a smaller ALL-CAPS title (TeXGyreAdventor,
11.6pt) on the next line within the same MuPDF block. The Category 3 fix
in `_render_heading_spans` (emit.py) joins bare-number line[0] with
subsequent lines, but only when font sizes match within 0.5pt. Here the
difference is 8.3pt, so line[1] ("CHANGELOG") is silently dropped.

Proposed fix: Relax the break condition from
  `abs(line.font_size - head_fs) > 0.5`
to
  `line.font_size > head_fs + 0.5`
This allows joining when the number is LARGER than the title (decorative
pattern) but still blocks when the title is larger than the number
(reference numbers, footnotes). The P4007R0 false-positive cases (running
headers classified as headings) are a separate Category 7 issue.

Simulation: 93 multi-font heading instances across 13 PDFs. The Kretz
pattern (fs=19.9 + fs=11.6) accounts for 80+ of these across P3844R3/R4,
P3932R0, P3948R1, P3978R0-R3, P4011R0, P4012R0/R1. The remaining cases
(P0876R22, P4007R0) have line[0] SMALLER than line[1] and would correctly
NOT be joined by the proposed fix.

Affected Papers (13):

